{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task is AGENT-TF-01, which involves implementing a Toolformer API-call filtering mechanism. Let me understand the requirements:\n\n1. For each call, compute: `gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call`\n2. Normalize gain by the number of prediction tokens: `normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens`\n3. A call is accepted if:\n   - `parseable == true`\n   - `normalized_gain \u003e= threshold`\n4. Return:\n   - `accepted_call_ids`: list of call_ids that are accepted, in source order\n   - `diagnostics`: list of per-call objects with `call_id`, `accepted`, `normalized_gain`, in source order\n\nLet me verify with the first test case:\n- threshold: 0.05\n- call0: gain = 1.94835097 - 0.38569502 = 1.56265595, normalized = 1.56265595/5 = 0.31253119, parseable=true → accepted\n- call1: gain = 1.06116273 - 0.68319969 = 0.37796304, normalized = 0.37796304/4 = 0.09449076, parseable=true → accepted\n- call2: gain = 1.21810502 - 0.47260371 = 0.74550131, normalized = 0.74550131/6 = 0.12425022, parseable=true → accepted\n- call3: gain = 1.05721833 - 0.29767903 = 0.7595393, normalized = 0.7595393/5 = 0.1519079 (wait, let me recompute: 1.05721833 - 0.29767903 = 0.7595393), normalized = 0.7595393/5 = 0.15190786, parseable=true → accepted\n- call4: gain = 1.06717367 - 0.85733566 = 0.20983801, normalized = 0.20983801/5 = 0.04196760, parseable=true → 0.04196760 \u003c 0.05 → NOT accepted\n- call5: gain = 1.66191711 - 0.89798497 = 0.76393214, normalized = 0.76393214/4 = 0.19098304, parseable=true → accepted\n\nSo accepted: call0, call1, call2, call3, call5\n\nThe candidate_artifact mentions \"rounded per-call diagnostics\" - I need to figure out the rounding. It doesn't specify exactly, but let me look at the schema - `normalized_gain` is just a number type, so perhaps we round to some decimal places. Looking at the artifact description: \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" - this is vague. I'll round to a reasonable number of decimal places, perhaps 8 or keep full precision. Actually, the schema says `\"type\": \"number\"` - maybe no specific rounding is needed. Let me not round, or round to something reasonable like 8 decimal places.\n\nActually, re-reading: \"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" - I'll round to 8 decimal places to match the precision of the input values.\n\nNow let me implement the `solve(case)` function:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        if prediction_tokens \u003c= 0:\n            raise ValueError(f\"prediction_tokens must be positive for call {call_id}\")\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\n        normalized_gain_rounded = round(normalized_gain, 8)\n        \n        accepted = parseable and (normalized_gain_rounded \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"accepted\": accepted,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain_rounded\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nWait, the artifact says \"Raise ValueError for an infeasible or structurally invalid case instead of silently repairing it.\" So I should validate required fields. Let me add validation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    # Validate required top-level fields\n    if \"threshold\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required field: threshold\")\n    if \"calls\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required field: calls\")\n    \n    threshold = case[\"threshold\"]\n    calls = case[\"calls\"]\n    \n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"calls must be a list\")\n    \n    diagnostics = []\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    \n    for call in calls:\n        # Validate required call fields\n        required_fields = [\"call_id\", \"loss_without_call\", \"loss_with_call\", \"prediction_tokens\", \"parseable\"]\n        for field in required_fields:\n            if field not in call:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Missing required field '{field}' in call\")\n        \n        call_id = call[\"call_id\"]\n        loss_without = call[\"loss_without_call\"]\n        loss_with = call[\"loss_with_call\"]\n        prediction_tokens = call[\"prediction_tokens\"]\n        parseable = call[\"parseable\"]\n        \n        if prediction_tokens \u003c= 0:\n            raise ValueError(f\"prediction_tokens must be positive for call {call_id}\")\n        \n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\n        normalized_gain_rounded = round(normalized_gain, 8)\n        \n        accepted = bool(parseable) and (normalized_gain_rounded \u003e= threshold)\n        \n        diagnostics.append({\n            \"call_id\": call_id,\n            \"accepted\": accepted,\n            \"normalized_gain\": normalized_gain_rounded\n        })\n        \n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    \n    return {\n        \"accepted_call_ids\": accepted_call_ids,\n        \"diagnostics\": diagnostics\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks correct. Let me verify with test case a-002 that has `parseable: false` for call4:\n- call4: gain = 1.35899862 - 0.11897463 = 1.24002399, normalized = 1.24002399/4 = 0.31000600, parseable=false → NOT accepted (even though gain is high)\n\nThat makes sense with the requirement \"Require both parseability and normalized gain at or above threshold.\"\n\nNow I need to format this as a JSON object with the `implementation` key containing the Python source.\n\nThe response format must be exactly:\n```json\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    ...\"}\n```\n\nLet me write the final response. I need to properly escape the Python code as a JSON string.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # Validate required top-level fields\\n    for field in (\\\"threshold\\\", \\\"calls\\\"):\\n        if field not in case:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Missing required field: {field}\\\")\\n\\n    threshold = case[\\\"threshold\\\"]\\n    calls = case[\\\"calls\\\"]\\n\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    required_call_fields = [\\n        \\\"call_id\\\",\\n        \\\"loss_without_call\\\",\\n        \\\"loss_with_call\\\",\\n        \\\"prediction_tokens\\\",\\n        \\\"parseable\\\",\\n    ]\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        for f in required_call_fields:\\n            if f not in call:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Missing required field '{f}' in call entry\\\")\\n\\n        call_id = call[\\\"call_id\\\"]\\n        loss_without = call[\\\"loss_without_call\\\"]\\n        loss_with = call[\\\"loss_with_call\\\"]\\n        prediction_tokens = call[\\\"prediction_tokens\\\"]\\n        parseable = call[\\\"parseable\\\"]\\n\\n        if not isinstance(prediction_tokens, (int, float)) or prediction_tokens \u003c= 0:\\n            raise ValueError(\\n                f\\\"prediction_tokens must be a positive number for call '{call_id}'\\\"\\n            )\\n\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\\n        normalized_gain_rounded = round(normalized_gain, 8)\\n\\n        accepted = bool(parseable) and (normalized_gain_rounded \u003e= threshold)\\n\\n        diagnostics.append(\\n            {\\n                \\\"call_id\\\": call_id,\\n                \\\"accepted\\\": accepted,\\n                \\\"normalized_gain\\\": normalized_gain_rounded,\\n            }\\n        )\\n\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"accepted_call_ids\\\": accepted_call_ids,\\n        \\\"diagnostics\\\": diagnostics,\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_014hP31zBPQcwj4yNILTSjAl","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2465},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2465,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":54,"output_tokens":2195,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1695},"service_tier":"standard"}}